diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index ff92be649ff3f610b38798b3310751534d032814..2fcbee85d183e309227564d96bb0772f042c35e5 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -3,3 +3,17 @@
 A small TypeScript library, with no runtime dependency, of building blocks for our services that store,
 exchange and update JSON: configuration files, API payloads and stored records. It is imported by the
 other projects of the team, so its behaviour must follow the published standards it implements.
+
+## API
+
+### `resolvePointer(document, pointer)`
+
+Returns the value that a JSON Pointer ([RFC 6901](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6901), sections 3 and 4)
+refers to in a JSON document. `""` refers to the whole document. It throws a `PointerError` when the pointer is
+not a valid JSON Pointer or does not resolve to a value (missing member, array index out of range, `-`, an index
+with a leading zero, or descending into a primitive). `null` is a value, not a missing one. Only own members are
+followed, and the document is not modified. The URI fragment form (section 6) is not supported.
+
+## Development
+
+`npm test` type-checks and builds with `tsc`, then runs the tests with `node --test`.
